<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 01_text_elements/09: Subscript and superscript -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Subscript and superscript</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .card { background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.12); }
    .formula { font-size: 1.5rem; font-family: Georgia, serif; }
    sup, sub { line-height: 0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Subscript and superscript</h1>
    <p class="lead">sub and sup for formulas, footnotes and ordinals.</p>
    <section class="card">
      <p class="formula">H<sub>2</sub>O &nbsp; CO<sub>2</sub> &nbsp; E = mc<sup>2</sup></p>
      <p>The 1<sup>st</sup>, 2<sup>nd</sup> and 3<sup>rd</sup> places.</p>
      <p>Light travels fast.<sup><a href="#note-1">1</a></sup></p>
      <p id="note-1"><small>1. About 3 &times; 10<sup>8</sup> metres per second.</small></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
